---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---

<BaseLayout title="About — System Design Log" description="Why this site exists and how to read it.">
  <p class="eyebrow">About</p>
  <h1>Why this site exists</h1>

  <div class="prose">
    <p>
      I'm a Senior Technical Program Manager at Cloudflare working in security engineering. I spend
      most of my time around systems rather than inside them, and I wanted a structured way to close
      that gap — so I started working through system design problems and writing down what I learned.
    </p>

    <div class="callout">
      <p>
        <strong>What this is not:</strong> a teaching resource. I'm not a subject matter expert on distributed
        systems, and nothing here should be treated as a reference implementation. These are my working
        notes, published as-is.
      </p>
    </div>

    <h2>How each write-up is structured</h2>
    <p>Every problem follows roughly the same shape, because the repetition is the point:</p>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Requirements</strong> — what the system has to do, and the constraints I assumed.</li>
      <li><strong>Estimates</strong> — rough traffic, storage, and bandwidth math to size the design.</li>
      <li><strong>Approach</strong> — the design I landed on and how data moves through it.</li>
      <li><strong>Tradeoffs</strong> — what I gave up, and the alternatives I rejected.</li>
      <li><strong>What I'd do differently</strong> — where my first pass was wrong.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>How it was built</h2>
    <p>
      The site is a static <a href="https://astro.build/">Astro</a> build, deployed to Cloudflare
      Pages from GitHub. I built it with <a href="https://claude.com/claude-code">Claude Code</a> —
      the write-ups themselves are mine, but the scaffolding, styling, and deploy pipeline were done
      in collaboration with an agent. That was partly the point: I wanted a working feel for what
      that workflow is actually like end to end.
    </p>
    <p>
      An earlier project on <a href="https://erichandal.me/">my portfolio</a> was built the same way
      using OpenAI Codex, so this doubles as a side-by-side comparison of the two.
    </p>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>
